
  <sn><md>### The Dot `.` in Regex

The dot matches `any single character except a newline`. It is the wildcard of regex: it doesn't care what the character is, only that `there is exactly one`.

```
Pattern:  c.t
Text:     "cat cot cut c9t c-t ct c t coat"
Matches:  cat, cot, cut, c9t, c-t,c t
```

`ct` fails because nothing sits between c and t. `coat` fails because two characters sit between them.
</md></sn>
